-威張る is a native verb whose reading is learned as a whole, but its parts can still be seen: 威 supplies い, which matches the KANJIDIC2 on reading イ, and 張 supplies ば, the voiced form of the は of 張る はる, "to stretch; to spread; to strain; to tighten," followed by る, the okurigana, the kana ending that follows the kanji. This voicing at the start of a second element is called rendaku. JMdict also lists the variant reading えばる for 威張る; え is not a KANJIDIC2 reading of 威, so it has no row here. In 威す, 威し and 威かす, 威 writes おど, followed by す, し or かす.
